# WHY EVERY ENTRY BELOW CARRIES AN EXPLICIT `=<40-hex sha>`
#
# `clone-siblings` resolves a BARE entry from the workspace lock, and raises
# NEED_LOCK for it -- which makes a missing lock FATAL. No lock is published
# for this repo's branch tip, so every reprobuild run died in `clone-siblings`
# with:
#
#     ::error::No workspace lock for isonim-tui (candidates: ...). Neither a
#     repo-workspaces locks/<project>/isonim-tui/<sha>.xml nor a reprobuild
#     locks/<project>/isonim-tui/<sha>.toml exists in
#     metacraft-labs/metacraft-manifests@latest.
#
# before a single dependency was provisioned. With no bare entry left, nothing
# needs a revision FROM the lock, so `lock_unavailable()` degrades to a
# `::warning::` and the clones proceed.
#
# Each SHA below is the tip of the ref that sibling's own repository actually
# uses as its default branch, verified to exist with `git ls-remote` (the refs
# are NOT uniformly `main` -- see the `@<branch>` note on each line).
#
# THIS IS THE FALLBACK, NOT THE GOAL. `clone-siblings.sh` prescribes it in
# that order: (1) declare these repos in isonim-tui's project manifest in
# metacraft-labs/metacraft-manifests so the lock pins them for every future
# commit with nothing to maintain; (2) only where (1) is impossible, name a
# 40-hex commit SHA here -- a commit, never a branch, because a branch tip is
# exactly the unpinned resolve the mechanism exists to prevent. Delete these
# `=<sha>` suffixes as soon as (1) lands.
#
# Cross-repo siblings cloned by setup-dev-env at the explicit SHAs
# pinned below (see codetracer-specs/Testing/Cross-Repo-CI-Integration.md).
#
# This list is the set of `--path:../<repo>/...` entries the Justfile's
# `src-paths` / `real-terminal-paths` and `config.nims` actually resolve.
# CI cloned none of them (bare `actions/checkout@v4`), which is why `just
# lint` produced tens of thousands of "cannot open file" errors and still
# reported success -- the recipes pipe into `tee` and just's default shell
# had no pipefail.

